,152,156,157,160,161,164],{},"Send any USSD request (",[153,154,155],"code",{},"*100#",", ",[153,158,159],{},"*111*0887#",", …) from the detail panel of a port, or to many ports\nat once from ",[142,162,163],{},"More → Bulk USSD",". The answer appears in the port's log.",[134,166,168],{"id":167},"own-number-and-balance-codes","Own-number and balance codes",[139,170,171,172,175,176,179,180,183],{},"The gateway knows the codes of many operators. For others, set them once in ",[142,173,174],{},"Settings → USSD\ncommands",", per operator (",[153,177,178],{},"MCC:MNC",", for example ",[153,181,182],{},"250:11","):",[185,186,187,194],"ul",{},[188,189,190,193],"li",{},[142,191,192],{},"Own number"," — the request whose answer contains the SIM's number; used when the SIM itself does\nnot store it.",[188,195,196,199],{},[142,197,198],{},"Balance"," — shown in the port details.",[139,201,202,203,206],{},"Removing an entry goes back to the built-in code. Noise in answers (prefixes, separators) is cleaned\nup automatically; extra patterns go to ",[142,204,205],{},"Settings → Numbers and IMSI",".",[134,208,210],{"id":209},"debug-tools","Debug tools",[139,212,213,216],{},[142,214,215],{},"Debug"," opens raw tools for a port that is not in work: an AT console with presets, Lua scripts,\nmodem probes, an SMS composer and the port's runtime state. Use them for diagnostics only: a port\nin the debug workspace is not selling.",[139,218,219],{},[220,221],"img",{"alt":222,"className":223,"src":225},"AT console",[224],"prose-shot","\u002Fscreenshots\u002Fen\u002F03_at_console.png",{"title":227,"searchDepth":228,"depth":228,"links":229},"",2,[230,231,232,233],{"id":136,"depth":228,"text":137},{"id":147,"depth":228,"text":148},{"id":167,"depth":228,"text":168},{"id":209,"depth":228,"text":210},"The SMS inbox of a port, USSD requests, and teaching the gateway an operator's own-number and balance codes.","md",null,{},{"icon":34},{"title":31,"description":234},"NGUND_xsQ3flhuTDVo5AeN3FmoXp5GRap0WyuhO5AQA",[242,244],{"title":26,"path":27,"description":243},"How a SIM becomes a number on sale, auto-connect, rent, and what the server's answers mean.",{"title":36,"path":37,"description":245},"The settings that matter day to day, grouped as in the app.",1794978314519]